From 71a1f53cc9b4e2f2be56a060fb5128f04d4b2831 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrice Brissette <pbrisset@cisco.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:26:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 121/123] zebra: don't map a VNI-less VLAN on a VLAN-aware
 bridge to an EVPN

On a VLAN-aware bridge, zebra_evpn_map_vlan() looked up the VLAN's VNI and,
when the VLAN had none, fell through to the walk meant for VLAN-unaware
bridges. That walk ignores the VLAN and returns the EVPN of the first VXLAN
device on the bridge, so a local MAC learned on a VLAN without a VNI was
handed to an unrelated EVPN instance.

On a VLAN-aware bridge the VLAN's access BD is authoritative, as it already
is in zebra_evpn_from_svi(): return no EVPN when the VLAN has no VNI.

Signed-off-by: Patrice Brissette <pbrisset@cisco.com>
---
 zebra/zebra_evpn.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/zebra/zebra_evpn.c b/zebra/zebra_evpn.c
index 945ec8541f..12622c5dd2 100644
--- a/zebra/zebra_evpn.c
+++ b/zebra/zebra_evpn.c
@@ -681,11 +681,10 @@ struct zebra_evpn *zebra_evpn_map_vlan(struct interface *ifp,
 	zif = br_if->info;
 	assert(zif);
 
-	/* Special case for vlan */
+	/* The VLAN's access BD is authoritative; the walk below ignores the VLAN. */
 	if (IS_ZEBRA_IF_BRIDGE_VLAN_AWARE(zif)) {
 		vni_id = zebra_l2_bridge_if_vni_find(zif, vid);
-		if (vni_id)
-			return zebra_evpn_lookup(vni_id);
+		return vni_id ? zebra_evpn_lookup(vni_id) : NULL;
 	}
 
 	in_param.vid = vid;
